      "source": [
        "## 5. Splitting Criteria: Gini vs Entropy :\n",
        "Gini and Entropy are two ways of measuring how mixed a group is. Both are tested at the same depth to compare the results."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fqNMbx3zDcpd"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "for crit in ['gini', 'entropy']:\n",
        "    m = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=5, criterion=crit, class_weight='balanced', random_state=42)\n",
        "    m.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "    print(f\"{crit:8s} -> Train: {m.score(X_train, y_train):.3f} | Test: {m.score(X_test, y_test):.3f}\")"
